module Core

# Each declaration below creates nothing: `@rf` names the shared declaration it shows, and validate-stdlib
# checks that the two still match.

### Represents the crashable raised when a numeric operation has no real-number
### result — an undefined or out-of-domain operation such as `0/0`, the logarithm
### of a non-positive value, `acos` of an argument outside `[-1, 1]`, or the square
### root of a negative value. Distinct from {NumericOverflowError} (the true result
### is finite but too large) and {DivisionByZeroError} (a nonzero value over zero).
@rf("NumericDomainError")
crashable NumericDomainError
    ### Stores a preformatted description of the domain error.
    description: Text

### Returns the stored numeric domain-error message.
### :returns: The resulting `Text` value.
@rf("NumericDomainError.crash_message")
routine NumericDomainError.crash_message() -> Text
